# LOB — UI / UX chrome

Apply when editing shell layout, brand marks, nav, or page chrome. Prefer existing brand components over new ad-hoc logos.

## Brand hierarchy (do not stack duplicates)

| Layer | Component | Role |
|-------|-----------|------|
| Global wordmark | `LobBrandMasthead` in `src/app/layout.tsx` | Full-bleed navy bar. Inner row `max-w-[1680px] mx-auto`. Centered full lockup (`lob-lockup-knockout.png`: nested-L mark \| gold rule \| LOB / LUMBER ONE BOARD). Favicon is mark-only (`src/app/icon.png`). No `#1` line in the masthead. |
| Primary nav | `AppNav` | Desktop: product link row + role pill + account. Mobile: account chrome only (product pages in bottom tabs). Guests: Create account and Sign in. **No** LOB mark in AppNav. |
| In-app sidebar | `LobSidebar` | Desktop: product name + slogan (`BRAND_POSITIONING`) above Navigate, then nav links. Admin links for `ADMIN`. |
| Status chrome | `RoleRibbon`, `AdminViewAsBar`, `DemoBanner` | Company and approval. Role pill stays in `AppNav` only. |

- **Global masthead** — one navy bar. Do not add another full-bleed wordmark above/beside `AppNav` or on sign-in.
- **Sidebar brand block** — keep “Lumber One Board” + “The #1 Lumber Load Board” above Navigate on desktop. That is intentional local wayfinding, not a second masthead.
- **Masthead lockup** — full logo knockout (`LOB_LOCKUP_KNOCKOUT_SRC`) centered in the rail. Do not use mark-only or the boxed `lob-app-icon.png` as the masthead logo. Favicon stays mark-only.
- **Masthead background is full-bleed** — `w-full` edge-to-edge navy; content lockup is rail-aligned.
- **No logo in `AppNav`**.
- **Commit buttons** use `lobWoodPrimaryButtonClass` (navy). Gold is an accent, not a gradient fill. Do not use emerald for Post, Book, or Export.
- **Do not** paint the page background by persona. `data-persona` may exist. The paper color stays shared.
- Reuse `@/components/lob-brand-*`, `LobWoodOIcon`, `@/lib/brand`, `@/lib/brand-marketing` — do not invent new lockups.

## UX defaults

- Match neighboring Tailwind patterns (stone/navy/gold tokens in `globals.css`).
- Public landing may show one example load row. Do not put the hero logo card back under the masthead.
- Account creation is one button, then Supplier or Carrier. Do not put four peer sign-in and sign-up buttons on the landing page.
- Mobile: the same compact lockup. Product links stay in the top scroller and the bottom bar.
- Minimal diffs — no drive-by redesign of unrelated surfaces.

## Ship

- UI/UX session changes land on **`origin/main`** (commit + push) so the existing Vercel project **`lob`** deploys — do not create a new Vercel project.
- Production aliases: `lob-damian-les-projects.vercel.app` (and related). Per-deploy `lob-*-damian-les-projects.vercel.app` URLs are snapshots of that same project.

## Entry points

- Shell: `src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/components/app-nav.tsx`, `src/components/lob-brand-masthead.tsx`
- Workspace chrome: `src/components/lob-sidebar.tsx`, `src/components/load-board-workspace.tsx`
- Tokens: `src/app/globals.css`, `src/lib/brand.ts`
